<title>DENMARK: DUTCH NCM BUYS DANISH EKR KREDITFORSIKRING.</title>
<headline>DUTCH NCM BUYS DANISH EKR KREDITFORSIKRING.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish credit insurance firm EKR Kreditforsikring A/S said on Wednesday it was to be wholly taken over by Dutch Nederlandsche Creditverzekering Maatschappij (NCM) effective January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>EKR has been 25 percent-owned by NCM since April 1995, ECR said in a statement, adding that the full takeover came in response to NCM's wish to link the Danish company more closely to the rest of NCM group.</p>
<p>EKR said the takeover deal was subject to approval by the finance committee of the Danish parliament.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
